cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the MAPFD-AL dataset, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MAPFD-AL: Estimating Maximum Annual Peak Flow Discharge for Gauged and Ungauged Streams in Alabama with a Hybrid MLR-XGBoost Model (NSF Water-R2O NRT 2023)"
abstract: >-
  Code and trained models that estimate maximum annual peak flow discharge for
  77,421 NHDPlusV2.1 stream reaches in Alabama, gauged and ungauged. Models were
  trained on peak flow records from 188 USGS gauges with channel geometry,
  catchment, soil, climate, and land-cover predictors. A hybrid approach uses
  XGBoost regression and falls back to a multiple linear regression (MLR) model
  where XGBoost gives non-physical values. Developed in the NSF Water-R2O NRT
  program at The University of Alabama and presented at the AWRA 2024 Spring
  Conference.
